<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Presence · Instrumentation Cost</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: #181818; background: #f5f5f3; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; }
    main { max-width: 1160px; margin: auto; padding: 56px 28px 80px; }
    header { border-top: 4px solid #181818; padding: 28px 0; }
    .eyebrow { font: 12px ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .15em; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 54px); letter-spacing: -.04em; margin: 20px 0; }
    h2 { font-size: 23px; letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 0 0 20px; }
    p, li { line-height: 1.65; max-width: 88ch; }
    a { color: inherit; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .intro { font-size: 19px; max-width: 68ch; }
    .note { border-left: 3px solid #333; padding: 12px 20px; background: #e9e9e6; }
    section { margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid #ccc; }
    .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: #fff; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    th, td { padding: 16px; text-align: right; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; white-space: nowrap; }
    th { background: #e9e9e6; font-size: 13px; }
    th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
    td strong { display: block; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; }
    td small { display: block; margin-top: 5px; color: #5c5c5c; font-size: 12px; }
    code, pre { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12px; }
    pre { background: #e9e9e6; padding: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; line-height: 1.7; }
    footer { margin-top: 48px; color: #666; font-size: 12px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body><main>
  <header>
    <div class="eyebrow">Transductive / Presence / Local Benchmark</div>
    <h1>The Cost of Seeing Inside.</h1>
    <p class="intro">Raw Bloom operations, the OTel wrapper between refreshes, and the synchronous operation that refreshes statistics.</p>
    <p>{{ caseCount }} measured cases · Java 21 · Murmur3 128 · One owner thread</p>
    <p><a href="results.json">Raw JMH JSON</a> · <a href="run.txt">Run Configuration</a> · <a href="jmh.log">Full JMH Log</a></p>
  </header>
  {% if smoke %}<p class="note"><strong>Smoke Run.</strong> This checks the harness only. Use the full run before drawing performance conclusions.</p>{% endif %}
  <p><strong>Read each cell:</strong> average nanoseconds per operation, JMH’s ±99.9% confidence error, and allocated bytes per operation. Lower is better. Values below 0.01 B/op are below this report’s display threshold; they do not prove zero allocation.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Raw:</strong> direct core operation with the same filter, input pool, and query selection.</li>
    <li><strong>No-Op Meter:</strong> wrapper delegation and the real monotonic clock check, without SDK recording.</li>
    <li><strong>SDK Recording:</strong> a real registered in-memory reader enables counter aggregation. No exporter, network, or concurrent collection is included.</li>
    <li><strong>SDK + Refresh:</strong> each operation takes the automatic refresh branch. A benchmark-only clock offset advances 30 seconds, retaining both real <code>System.nanoTime()</code> reads. That offset increment and additions are included in the score.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note"><strong>Refresh is deliberately amplified.</strong> These are warm-cache average costs when every call refreshes, not p99 latency or a simulation of a 30-second production cadence. Between-refresh cases use the default interval and reset it outside each short iteration. Fixed statistics currently scan the bit array three times; scalable statistics use slice counters.</p>
  {% for section in sections %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ section.title }}</h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Inserted Values</th><th>Raw</th><th>No-Op Meter</th><th>SDK Recording</th><th>SDK + Refresh</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{% for row in section.rows %}<tr>
        <td>{{ row.n }}</td>
        {% for name in ["raw", "noopMeter", "sdkRecording", "sdkRefreshing"] %}
        <td><strong>{{ row[name].score }} ns</strong><small>± {{ row[name].error }} ns</small><small>{{ row[name].allocation }} B/op</small></td>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
    </table></div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
  <section>
    <h2>What Is in Memory</h2>
    <p>Fixed capacity equals N. Scalable starts at 1,000 and grows under the same 1% target. Payload excludes object headers, telemetry, and the 8,192-query pool. Absent queries are never inserted; false positives remain in the timings. Present queries sample all insertion ages. Repeated puts keep occupancy stable and do not measure fresh insertion, layer growth, or first-series registration.</p>
    <div class="scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Filter</th><th>Inserted Values</th><th>Layers</th><th>Bit-Array Bytes</th><th>False Positives / Absent Pool</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{% for fixture in fixtures %}<tr><td>{{ fixture.kind }}</td><td>{{ fixture.n }}</td><td>{{ fixture.layers }}</td><td>{{ fixture.bytes }}</td><td>{{ fixture.falsePositives }} / {{ fixture.queries }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p>Inputs are prebuilt, fixed-length ASCII strings. No value construction is timed. Bloom hashing does not use or cache <code>String.hashCode()</code>. These results isolate instrumentation on a bounded query working set; they are not a comparison with Java collections or a production throughput forecast.</p>
  </section>
  <section><h2>Reproduce Locally</h2><pre>mise run benchmark:otel
# Select different sizes (minimum 1,000):
mise run benchmark:otel -- -PbenchmarkSizes=1000,10000,100000</pre>
    <pre>{{ environment }}</pre>
    <p>Warmup and measurement run in separate JVM forks with JMH’s GC profiler. Background desktop or container work can affect timing. Confidence intervals describe this run, not reproducibility across machines. Generated reports stay in the ignored build directory.</p>
  </section>
  <footer>Presence / Theory Meets The Machine</footer>
</main></body></html>
